                    <birth when="1000">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1817-03-12"/>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
    Godwin noted the execution of John Cashman who had taken an active part in the assault and plunder of Mr Beckwith’s 
    gunsmith shop in Skinner Street where Godwin also had his premises. The assault took place on 2 December 1816, after which the mob had marched to the Tower of London to 
    try and persuade troops to join them.  Cashman was hanged in front of Beckwith’s shop.  </note>
                    <bibl type="journalism"><title>The Times</title>, 13 March 1817</bibl>
